agents.prompt:
Extract and clarify the raw idea.

Idea: {{idea}}
Project: {{project}}
Module: {{module}}
Context: {{context}}

Your task:
1. Restate the idea in one sentence (core value proposition)
2. Identify 3-5 key constraints or assumptions
3. List known adjacent modules or related features in the project
4. Identify gaps or unknowns that need clarification
5. Suggest a short slug for this feature (e.g. 'email-verification', 'dark-mode')

Return JSON: { "title": "", "one_liner": "", "key_assumptions": [], "adjacent_modules": [], "unknowns": [], "slug": "" }

Research related specs and existing work.

Idea: {{idea}}
Title: {{idea-extractor.title}}
Adjacent modules: {{idea-extractor.adjacent_modules}}
Project: {{project}}

Your task:
1. List 3-5 related features or components that may intersect with this idea
2. For each, explain the relationship (depends-on, conflicts-with, or independent)
3. Flag any in-progress work that might affect this idea
4. Suggest a unique spec ID (format: SPEC-{{project}}-{{module}}-NN)
5. Identify any blockers or prerequisites

Return JSON: { "related_features": [{"name": "", "relation": "depends-on|conflicts-with|independent", "explanation": ""}], "suggested_id": "", "blockers": [], "in_progress_related": [] }

Analyze integration points with existing system modules.

Idea: {{idea}}
Title: {{idea-extractor.title}}
Related features: {{spec-researcher.related_features}}
Project: {{project}}

Your task:
1. For each adjacent module from the research phase, identify 1-2 integration points
2. Suggest how this feature could leverage or extend existing modules
3. Flag any architectural contradictions or risks
4. Identify which existing APIs, data models, or events this feature would interact with
5. Assess implementation complexity (low / medium / high) with a brief rationale

Return JSON: { "integration_points": [{"module": "", "points": [], "suggestion": ""}], "architecture_risks": [], "api_dependencies": [], "complexity": "low|medium|high", "complexity_rationale": "" }

Review the proposed feature scope against the target version constraints.

Idea: {{idea}}
Target version: {{target_version}}
Integration points: {{cross-analyzer.integration_points}}
Architecture risks: {{cross-analyzer.architecture_risks}}
Blockers: {{spec-researcher.blockers}}

Your task:
1. For each integration point, check: is this dependency available NOW, or does it require a system that does not yet exist?
2. Flag features requiring non-existent external systems as OUT_OF_SCOPE for the target version
3. Propose a reduced scope deliverable in {{target_version}} without non-existent dependencies
4. List deferred features with suggested future version

Return JSON: { "in_scope": [], "out_of_scope": [{"feature": "", "reason": "", "defer_to": ""}], "reduced_scope_summary": "", "deferred_features": [] }

Draft a structured feature specification.

Idea: {{idea}}
Title: {{idea-extractor.title}}
One-liner: {{idea-extractor.one_liner}}
Spec ID: {{spec-researcher.suggested_id}}
Project: {{project}}
Module: {{module}}
Priority: {{priority}}
Complexity: {{cross-analyzer.complexity}}
In-scope features: {{scope-guardian.in_scope}}
Deferred (out of scope): {{scope-guardian.out_of_scope}}
Integration points: {{cross-analyzer.integration_points}}
Blockers: {{spec-researcher.blockers}}

Your task: Produce a complete feature specification in the following format:

```
id: [spec_id]
title: [clear title]
status: draft
priority: [1-5]
project: [project]
module: [module]
complexity: [low|medium|high]

DONE-WHEN:
- [measurable acceptance criterion 1]
- [measurable acceptance criterion 2]
- [measurable acceptance criterion 3]

CONTEXT:
[2-3 sentences: why this matters, user value, business case]

ARCHITECTURE:
[Key design decisions, data structures, API contracts, module interactions]

DEPENDENCIES:
[Blocking items, required integrations, prerequisite features]

OPEN QUESTIONS:
[Decisions to resolve before implementation starts]

IMPLEMENTATION NOTES:
[Suggested approach, phasing, edge cases to handle]
```

Return plain text (markdown code block).
